gpu/buddy: drop a free block from the free tree before rollback coalescing

When a range allocation fails after splitting, the rollback path coalesces
the block with its buddy. A block that is still marked free remains linked
in its free tree, so the merge frees metadata that the tree still points to.
Remove the block from the tree before merging.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/buddy.c b/drivers/gpu/buddy.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/buddy.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/buddy.c
@@ -248,6 +248,9 @@
 {
 	struct gpu_buddy_block *parent;
 	unsigned int order;
+
+	if (gpu_buddy_block_is_free(block) && !RB_EMPTY_NODE(&block->rb))
+		rbtree_remove(mm, block);

 	while ((parent = block->parent)) {
 		struct gpu_buddy_block *buddy;
